      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Linear Linked list has a drawback that we we can\nonly traverse nodes after one node but not reach the\npreveious node .\n\n2. To overcome this drawback we can store the\naddress of first node to last node .\n\n3. That is now last node point to the first node .\n\n4. In this way we can traverse the whole linkedlist\nstarting from any node .\n\n4. Such LinkedList is called circular LinkedList .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Linear Linked list has a drawback that we we can only traverse nodes after one node but not reach the preveious node .\n\n2. To overcome this drawback we can store the address of first node to last node .\n\n3. That is now last node point to the first node .\n\n4. In this way we can traverse the whole linkedlist starting from any node .\n\n4. Such LinkedList is called circular LinkedList .",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
